RLK
---

Minimal C99 grid library for roguelikes and 2D grid-based games. A companion
to [PXL](https://github.com/pirmd/pxl): RLK owns the game grid (cells, tiles,
viewports/cameras); PXL owns the pixels. RLK itself is graphics-backend
agnostic and has no rendering dependency.

Features:
  - Grid: 2D array of tile cells with bounds-safe get/set, fill, fill_rect
  - View: a clamped camera/window onto a grid (origin + size in cells),
          with center/move helpers and cell-to-grid mapping
  - Backend agnostic: rendering is left to the user / a companion lib
  - Minimal C99, header-friendly public API, strict-warning clean
  - Unit tests + a PXL-backed demo

Build:
  make          # Build librlk.a
  make lint     # Static analysis with strict warnings (-Werror)
  make test     # Run unit tests
  make demo     # Build demos (requires PXL, see below)
  make clean    # Remove build artifacts

Build configuration:
  Main configuration is defined in Makefile.inc.
  Copy 'config.mk.example' to 'config.mk' to override CFLAGS or the PXL
  location used by the demo.

PXL for the demo:
  The demo links against PXL, RLK's companion graphics library. Either place
  a pxl checkout at ../pxl (the default) or set PXL_DIR in config.mk:

    cp config.mk.example config.mk
    # PXL_DIR = /path/to/pxl
    # PXL_BACKEND = sdl    # x11 (default) or sdl

  Then build pxl (see the pxl README), and from rlk:

    make demo

Quick start:
    /* Build and show a grid through a PXL-backed view */
    rlk_grid_t map;
    rlk_grid_init(&map, 40, 30);
    rlk_grid_fill(&map, TILE_FLOOR);
    rlk_grid_fill_rect(&map, 0, 0, 40, 1, TILE_WALL);

    rlk_view_t view;
    rlk_view_init(&view, &map, 0, 0, 32, 28);
    rlk_view_center(&view, 20, 15);

    /* In your render loop: */
    for (int vy = 0; vy < view.vh; ++vy)
      for (int vx = 0; vx < view.vw; ++vx) {
        rlk_tile_t t = rlk_view_get(&view, vx, vy);
        /* ...draw a TILE_PX square for t with your renderer (e.g. PXL)... */
      }

    rlk_grid_deinit(&map);

  See demo/demo_grid.c for a complete PXL-backed example.

Demos:
  - demo_grid.c - Renders an rlk grid with PXL: a small dungeon, a panning
                  view, arrow-key camera, ESC to quit.

Architecture:
  Core:
    err.h   - Error codes
    grid.h  - Grid: 2D tile array (get/set/fill/fill_rect), bounds-safe
    view.h  - View: clamped camera window onto a grid (map/center/move)
  rlk.h - umbrella header that includes all public headers.

Testing:
  Framework: test/test.h (minimalist assert-based testing).
  Run tests: make test.

